1
00:00:16,430 --> 00:00:17,510
[Eita, I entrust this to you]
[The truth, of the day I broke]

2
00:00:17,510 --> 00:00:18,510
[But the key to 203]
[is the one thing I can't give you]

3
00:01:02,670 --> 00:01:06,700
I'm sorry about yesterday.

4
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:09,010
Don't apologize.

5
00:01:11,490 --> 00:01:15,620
You should try making
that soup from yesterday.

6
00:01:16,540 --> 00:01:17,560
Huh?

7
00:01:17,560 --> 00:01:20,380
If it's your recipe, I'd love to try it.

8
00:01:36,550 --> 00:01:38,070
Today's your day off, right?

9
00:01:38,070 --> 00:01:40,860
- Yeah.
- Relax, and take it easy.

10
00:01:40,860 --> 00:01:43,650
- See you later.
- See you.

11
00:01:45,370 --> 00:01:52,150
[These are sketches you left behind]
[I couldn't throw them away]

12
00:02:15,980 --> 00:02:18,450
I drew this?

13
00:02:28,540 --> 00:02:30,660
Hello?

14
00:02:30,660 --> 00:02:32,790
<i>Did you get the package?</i>

15
00:02:32,790 --> 00:02:36,220
Yeah. Did I draw all of these?

16
00:02:36,220 --> 00:02:41,220
<i>Yup. Seems like the manager
held onto them for you.</i>

17
00:02:42,470 --> 00:02:46,000
<i>How are things going with Eita?</i>

18
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:49,040
<i>You two are getting married soon, right?</i>

19
00:02:49,040 --> 00:02:51,580
We haven't talked about that yet.

20
00:02:52,170 --> 00:02:53,810
<i>Why not?</i>

21
00:02:53,810 --> 00:02:57,630
<i>Eita's dependable, and has a stable future.</i>

22
00:02:57,630 --> 00:03:00,680
<i>He understands and cares for you as well.</i>

23
00:03:02,180 --> 00:03:04,160
Mom.

24
00:03:05,520 --> 00:03:08,320
I had gotten into an accident, right?

25
00:03:08,320 --> 00:03:10,410
With a man named Lun.

26
00:03:10,410 --> 00:03:12,930
<i>Who told you?</i>

27
00:03:12,930 --> 00:03:15,130
You knew.

28
00:03:15,130 --> 00:03:18,710
<i>Sakura. You don't have to remember, okay?</i>

29
00:03:18,710 --> 00:03:20,850
Why?

30
00:03:20,850 --> 00:03:27,330
<i>You don't know what it was like for you
after the accident.</i>

31
00:03:28,050 --> 00:03:30,740
<i>You'd call me night after night,</i>

32
00:03:30,740 --> 00:03:33,460
<i>crying about how you couldn't breathe.</i>

33
00:03:33,460 --> 00:03:38,090
<i>Only to forget you called
by the next morning.</i>

34
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:42,930
But... But these are my memories.

35
00:03:42,930 --> 00:03:44,820
<i>Exactly.</i>

36
00:03:44,820 --> 00:03:49,070
<i>You said it yourself.
That you didn't want to remember.</i>

37
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:55,370
<i>Eita was there for you the entire time.</i>

38
00:03:58,180 --> 00:04:01,310
Are you saying
I should entrust everything to Eita?

39
00:04:01,310 --> 00:04:06,740
<i>Not everyone is so blessed to have
someone like that in their life.</i>

40
00:04:12,980 --> 00:04:14,970
I know.

41
00:04:29,010 --> 00:04:32,350
You haven't gotten any work done.

42
00:04:32,350 --> 00:04:33,910
Were you watching?

43
00:04:33,910 --> 00:04:36,040
I don't need to watch to tell.

44
00:04:38,370 --> 00:04:40,420
So you didn't give it to her.

45
00:04:41,580 --> 00:04:43,650
I couldn't.

46
00:04:44,630 --> 00:04:46,550
I see.

47
00:04:48,560 --> 00:04:51,500
Maybe I'll just put it in a safe.

48
00:04:51,500 --> 00:04:53,130
What?

49
00:04:53,130 --> 00:04:55,610
If I have it on hand,
I'll be tempted to give it to her.

50
00:04:56,380 --> 00:04:58,560
You don't want to give it to her?

51
00:05:00,320 --> 00:05:02,040
I don't know.

52
00:05:02,740 --> 00:05:05,130
I don't get you sometimes.

53
00:05:14,650 --> 00:05:18,070
What would you do, Natsume?
Would you pull back?

54
00:05:19,670 --> 00:05:23,650
I'd tell them not to go.

55
00:05:23,650 --> 00:05:25,100
What?

56
00:05:25,100 --> 00:05:30,040
I wouldn't be able to tell someone I love
that they were free to go wherever.

57
00:05:31,770 --> 00:05:34,010
Most people would agree.

58
00:05:35,180 --> 00:05:36,630
[White pepper soup, only on rainy days]

59
00:05:36,630 --> 00:05:39,000
<i>I'm not doing this to remember.</i>

60
00:05:40,780 --> 00:05:42,740
<i>I'm doing this for closure.</i>

61
00:05:47,820 --> 00:05:50,730
Today is special secret recipe!

62
00:05:50,730 --> 00:05:54,070
What? You said yesterday was secret.

63
00:05:54,070 --> 00:05:56,400
Today is very secret!

64
00:05:56,400 --> 00:05:59,460
Okay, okay. Really secret. I won't ask.

65
00:05:59,460 --> 00:06:02,180
The secret is...

66
00:06:03,100 --> 00:06:04,710
Huh?

67
00:06:04,710 --> 00:06:06,630
Now I know everything!

68
00:06:06,630 --> 00:06:08,410
Forget it!

69
00:06:08,410 --> 00:06:10,590
Nope. Nuh-uh.

70
00:06:10,590 --> 00:06:13,090
I remember now.

71
00:06:24,120 --> 00:06:27,020
<i>I just wanted to end things.</i>

72
00:06:35,970 --> 00:06:41,120
[Eita: I'll be coming home earlier today]

73
00:06:41,120 --> 00:06:45,410
[Is there anything you want to eat?]

74
00:06:45,410 --> 00:06:49,980
[I made soup]

75
00:06:56,640 --> 00:07:01,610
[Don't leave the vase empty]

76
00:07:20,850 --> 00:07:22,840
You didn't erase it.

77
00:07:26,610 --> 00:07:28,650
If I did,

78
00:07:30,500 --> 00:07:32,680
I'd only draw it again.

79
00:07:45,310 --> 00:07:46,710
Lei.

80
00:07:50,030 --> 00:07:54,780
I want you to hold onto this for me.

81
00:07:55,580 --> 00:07:59,190
You're going to use me,
to stop yourself from seeing her?

82
00:07:59,190 --> 00:08:00,800
No.

83
00:08:01,980 --> 00:08:04,560
I just don't want to hurt you anymore.

84
00:08:10,160 --> 00:08:12,270
Does that mean...

85
00:08:21,670 --> 00:08:23,620
You chose me?

86
00:08:55,770 --> 00:08:57,360
Lun.

87
00:09:08,850 --> 00:09:10,630
I love you.

88
00:09:34,920 --> 00:09:37,690
But I'm no replacement
for someone you want to forget.

89
00:09:41,160 --> 00:09:43,450
Hold onto this key yourself.

90
00:09:56,870 --> 00:10:00,620
Yesterday, I bumped into her fiancé at 203.

91
00:10:02,230 --> 00:10:04,220
All these years,

92
00:10:06,070 --> 00:10:08,220
I thought she cast you aside.

93
00:10:09,640 --> 00:10:11,390
But I was wrong.

94
00:10:12,420 --> 00:10:15,860
After the accident, she had slowly forgotten
all her memories with you.

95
00:10:18,490 --> 00:10:20,240
What?

96
00:10:29,380 --> 00:10:34,650
Is it my fault she forgot?

97
00:10:35,920 --> 00:10:37,950
I don't know.

98
00:10:40,390 --> 00:10:42,320
Go find that answer yourself.

99
00:10:42,930 --> 00:10:45,690
Why do you still encourage me
to look for her?

100
00:10:46,670 --> 00:10:48,500
I...

101
00:10:50,690 --> 00:10:54,620
I don't want to be your choice,

102
00:10:55,320 --> 00:10:57,470
while you still know nothing.

103
00:10:59,240 --> 00:11:01,640
If you want to end things,

104
00:11:03,350 --> 00:11:05,800
end them on your own terms.

105
00:11:08,350 --> 00:11:10,090
Then, once you're ready,

106
00:11:13,320 --> 00:11:15,250
come back to me,

107
00:11:16,780 --> 00:11:18,420
and give me your answer.

108
00:11:41,050 --> 00:11:43,020
- Hello!
- Hello.

109
00:11:43,020 --> 00:11:45,570
Are you looking for something?

110
00:11:45,570 --> 00:11:48,820
This one is popular.
Would you like to take a look?

111
00:11:51,250 --> 00:11:52,900
Oh, do you want a Eustoma​?

112
00:11:52,900 --> 00:11:55,110
- Yes.
- Sure!

113
00:11:55,110 --> 00:11:58,670
<i>I'm only going to leave these.
I won't see him.</i>

114
00:12:12,030 --> 00:12:15,000
[Eita: Just finished work, heading back now]

115
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:21,910
[Okay, I'll be waiting]

116
00:12:22,930 --> 00:12:24,810
<i>I have to get home.</i>

117
00:12:34,600 --> 00:12:35,990
Lun.

118
00:12:44,960 --> 00:12:46,670
Why are you here?

119
00:13:10,340 --> 00:13:12,950
I came to leave the keys behind.

120
00:13:14,380 --> 00:13:17,010
We came to end this.

121
00:13:17,010 --> 00:13:18,450
Yeah.

122
00:13:30,210 --> 00:13:32,660
I'll go back to Eita.

123
00:13:33,780 --> 00:13:36,120
You go back to Lei.

124
00:13:36,120 --> 00:13:37,580
Yeah.

125
00:13:38,770 --> 00:13:41,390
I have to go back to her.

126
00:13:41,390 --> 00:13:43,140
We have to.

127
00:13:52,190 --> 00:13:56,720
I... didn't want to see you.

128
00:13:56,720 --> 00:13:58,100
I know.

129
00:13:59,280 --> 00:14:03,450
I really... didn't want to see you.

130
00:14:05,590 --> 00:14:06,990
Yeah.

131
00:14:08,150 --> 00:14:09,770
But...

132
00:14:11,520 --> 00:14:13,810
I wanted to see you.

133
00:14:15,220 --> 00:14:19,430
Now, I don't know where to go.

134
00:14:28,820 --> 00:14:32,040
I don't know either.

135
00:14:34,130 --> 00:14:37,970
But I want to know who you are now.

136
00:14:37,970 --> 00:14:39,770
Did you remember?

137
00:14:39,770 --> 00:14:41,190
No.

138
00:14:44,380 --> 00:14:46,470
It's not that I remember.

139
00:15:47,080 --> 00:15:54,970
[Eita: I just got back, where are you?]

140
00:16:00,190 --> 00:16:04,490
[Eita, Location]

141
00:16:05,970 --> 00:16:09,730
[You've stopped sharing your location
with this individual]

142
00:16:15,520 --> 00:16:22,290
[Eita: I'll heat up your soup for us]

143
00:16:26,680 --> 00:16:28,380
You okay?

144
00:16:28,380 --> 00:16:29,740
Yeah.

145
00:17:17,150 --> 00:17:21,210
<i>I'll leave the door open when I'm home.</i>

146
00:19:00,830 --> 00:19:02,940
<i>At the zoo...</i>

147
00:19:02,940 --> 00:19:04,580
<i>Yeah?</i>

148
00:19:04,580 --> 00:19:09,560
<i>One animal went outside, but ran right back.</i>

149
00:19:10,820 --> 00:19:13,560
<i>Because it was scared?</i>

150
00:19:13,560 --> 00:19:14,990
<i>Yeah.</i>

151
00:19:16,150 --> 00:19:20,600
<i>But once they knew outside,
going back is different.</i>

152
00:19:21,850 --> 00:19:23,420
<i>You too?</i>

153
00:19:25,230 --> 00:19:26,830
<i>I don't know.</i>

154
00:19:28,810 --> 00:19:30,620
<i>Sakura...</i>

155
00:19:31,540 --> 00:19:37,130
<i>You won't suddenly disappear, right?</i>

156
00:20:12,500 --> 00:20:15,530
[Eita Nishikido]

157
00:20:51,960 --> 00:20:53,550
Don't move.

158
00:21:13,450 --> 00:21:15,380
I know this.

159
00:21:20,070 --> 00:21:22,180
Sakura?

160
00:21:22,180 --> 00:21:24,140
Don't come any closer.

161
00:21:27,050 --> 00:21:28,840
I'm sorry.

162
00:21:47,640 --> 00:21:50,560
- Sakura...
- Don't touch me!

163
00:23:01,570 --> 00:23:09,330
[Next]
